WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.030
This lesson covers eye and gut changes that you should report.

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:09.480
Eye symptoms can need fast attention.

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:15.900
Watch for eye pain, very red eyes, light sensitivity, or blurred or changing vision.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:20.430
These need urgent assessment, the same day.

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:23.010
Do not wait for a routine visit.

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:27.390
Seek emergency care for a loss of vision.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:31.920
These symptoms have several possible causes.

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:36.810
An eye exam is needed. The app cannot diagnose uveitis.

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:43.110
Getting treated early helps avoid long-term problems, like vision loss.

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:50.830
Tell your care team about ongoing gut pain, bloating, or changes in bowel habits.

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:58.210
IBD can happen alongside PsA, but a bowel change does not prove it is the cause.

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:01.060
Describe what changed, and when.

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:07.770
If symptoms are severe, or you feel very unwell, get urgent medical help.

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:11.840
Great job! Let’s review.

00:01:12.190 --> 00:01:18.720
New eye pain, marked redness, light sensitivity, or blurred sight need urgent assessment.

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:21.900
Seek emergency care for a loss of vision.
